  "regions": [
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "and compare the English phrase “thorn in the side.” अनक्षर = न अक्षरं",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "शास्त्रं यस्मिंस्तत्तथा says Râmarshi. It means, I think, “that which cannot",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "speak i. e. speak well.” Comp. ‘unlettered’ ‘illiterate’ in English.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "About the नृपाङ्गणगतः खलः Râmarshi has this तथा गतश्चेत्तर्हि सर्वप्राणिनां",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "मूलान्यपि निकृन्तति तस्य महापापरूपत्वात्. This Stanza occurs at p. 7 of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "the Kâvyasangraha.—Pṛithvî.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. LVII.—नामेति संभावनायाम् says Râmarshi.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. LVIII.—Here is another instance of Bhartṛihari’s condens-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "ed style, ‘one is dumb through taciturnity (i. e. one who talks",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "little is called dumb) ; clever at speech, a flatterer or a garrulous",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "fellow (i. e. one is so called if clever in speaking). अप्रगल्भः =",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "modest, timid comp. Bhaṭṭi. II., 15. For the form चाटुल see",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "Siddh. Kaum. I., 180. For the Genitive of योगिनाम् see Siddh.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "Kaum. I., 305. वातकी which is one variant for चाटुलो is explained by",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "Râmarshi to mean वातरोगी. अभिजातः the same commentator",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "renders by कुलीनो दक्षो वा. The former is the true meaning. No au-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "thority is given for the latter.—Mandâkrântâ.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. LIX.—खल. The commentator explains this as meaning",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "खलत्व, but the usual meaning will suit here. Wicked persons, boon",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "companions, are meant. Râmarshi, I find, agrees with this",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "interpretation. प्राग्जात &c = “whose indulgence in his wicked con-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "duct commenced before is now developed.” Râmarshi says प्राग्जाता",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "पूर्वमनुभूता विस्मृता विस्मरं प्रापिता निजा आत्मीया अधमा निकृष्टा कर्मवृत्तिः कर्मणा",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "जीविका येन स तथा but goes no further. This however is not quite clear",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "and on more than one point requires justification.—Vasantatilakâ.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. LX.—पूर्वार्ध &c. = distinguished by (i. e. as belonging to) the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "first half and the second half. See Siddh. Kaum. I., 273.—Upajâti.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r8",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. LXI.—संतोष. The commentator says सज्जना यदृच्छया लाभेन",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "संतुष्टाः.—which is no doubt the meaning. But it is noteworthy",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "that संतोष is co-ordinated with तृण and जल.—Âryâ",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
